A primary challenge in modern air defense design is the cost asymmetry between offensive strike assets and defensive interceptors. Adversaries can deploy low-cost threat vectors—such as unguided artillery rockets, long-range loitering munitions, and modified commercial drones—at minimal cost, while traditional defensive systems rely on complex precision-guided interceptors.OFFENSIVE THREAT VECTOR                 DEFENSIVE INTERCEPTOR COST


